{
  "format": "candid-profile",
  "format_version": 0,
  "kind": "contract",
  "name": "usdc-base-sepolia",
  "origin": "third_party",
  "language": "en",
  "description": "USDC's EIP-3009 messages on Base Sepolia, a test network (spec section 15.9, experimental), with the usdc profile's words. TransferWithAuthorization and ReceiveWithAuthorization pay `to` once, by a signature that someone else submits (only the payee, for ReceiveWithAuthorization), and CancelAuthorization cancels one that is unused (EIP-3009; Circle stablecoin-evm, FiatTokenV2.sol). x402's `exact` scheme pays by TransferWithAuthorization by default (coinbase/x402, specs/schemes/exact/scheme_exact_evm.md). Only the messages are described: USDC's ABI names transferWithAuthorization, receiveWithAuthorization, cancelAuthorization and permit twice each, which the resolver refuses (O1). Base Sepolia's USDC signs under the domain name `USDC`, not the mainnets' `USD Coin`, and a profile binds one domain, so it has a profile of its own. Read on chain on 2026-10-30 (DOMAIN_SEPARATOR, decimals 6, the three type hashes); x402's own examples use it.",
